# BuildKit resolves <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore in preference to
# <context>/.dockerignore, so this file governs the build WITHOUT putting a
# .dockerignore at the repo root -- nothing else in the repo is affected, and
# this travels with the Dockerfile it belongs to.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: the build context is the REPO ROOT, which is ~9 GB on the dev
# machine (apps/*/build, release/, node_modules). The Dockerfile COPYs nothing
# from the repo -- the toolchain is pinned by version, not by file -- so the
# whole context is excluded.
*
